    <!--
        Sample starter data - ~5 rows per table, in FK dependency order.
        All seeded users share the password: Passw0rd!
        (bcrypt hash below, cost 10, generated offline - matches what
        Spring Security's default BCryptPasswordEncoder produces/reads).

        Only runs once (tracked in databasechangelog, like every other
        changeset here). If you already created rows with the same
        natural keys by hand (e.g. a topic literally named "Travel" -
        the TESTING-GUIDE.md examples use that exact name), the unique
        constraint on topics.name / users.username will make this fail.
        Safest: reset the DB first (docker compose down -v && up -d)
        so this applies to a clean schema.
    -->

